* the derivation
	* proposition
		* KE = (m * c^2) * (y - 1)
	* proof
		* KE
		* = 
			* by the work done to accelerate an object from speed 0
		* sum (from 0 to x-end) (F * dx)
		* =
		* m * sum (by x) (from 0 to x-end)  (y^3 * a * x)
			* where y = 1 / (1 - v-end^2 / c^2)
		* =
			* a * dx = (dv / dt) * dx = dv * dx / dt = v * dv
		* m * sum (by v) (from 0 to v-end) (y^3 * v * v)
		* =
			* z := 1 - v^2 / c^2
				* then
					* z-start = 1
					* 
						* dz / dt = (-2/c^2) * v * (dv / dt)
						* dz = (-2/c^2) * v * dv
						* v * dv = (-1/2) * c^2 * dz
		* (- m * c^2 / 2) * sum (by z) (from 1 to z-end) (z^(-3/2))
		* =
		* (- m * c^2 / 2) * lift2 (-) (z^(-1/2) / (-1/2)) z-end 1
		* =
			* cancelling constants
		* (m * c^2) * lift2 (-) (z^(-1/2))) z-end 1
		* =
		* (m * c^2) * (1 / sqrt (1 - v-end^2 / c^2) - 1)
		* =
		* (m * c^2) * (y - 1)
* connection with the classical case is when v is small
	* (as v converges down to 0) (relativistic KE being close to classical KE)
	* is equivalent to
	* (as x converges down to 0) ((1 / sqrt (1 - x) - 1) being close to (x / 2))
		* x playing as (v^2/ c^2)
